# ==========================================================================
# Het Koersbord — what never leaves this machine
#
# The first rule matters more than all the others: this is a personal
# finance application, and backend/portfolio.db is not a build artefact. It
# holds every transaction, every position you have ever held, and your FRED
# and news API keys in the `setting` table. Git keeps history forever, so a
# database committed once stays recoverable even after it is deleted in a
# later commit — and a private repository can be made public by one click.
#
# The database is synced between machines by copying the file, never by git.
# See SETUP.md.
# ==========================================================================

# --- your data -----------------------------------------------------------
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3

# DEGIRO exports and anything else tabular. Broad on purpose: a stray
# Transactions.csv in the project root is your whole trading history.
# If you ever genuinely need to commit a CSV, force it:  git add -f the-file
*.csv
*.xlsx
*.xls

# POL: the politician tracker's filings (tens of thousands of PDFs), its database
# and its logs. Rebuilt by its own pipeline; never versioned.
backend/ptt/data/

# --- credentials ---------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
*.key
*.pem
secrets*.json

# --- Python --------------------------------------------------------------
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# --- Node / Next.js ------------------------------------------------------
node_modules/
.next/
out/
.vercel/
npm-debug.log*

# --- working files -------------------------------------------------------
# Screenshots and scratch output. Remove this line if you want them versioned.
Claude outputs/

# ERN: the documents and prompt each Claude Code report was written from,
# and your thesis with them. Rebuilt on demand; private.
ern_work/
# ALRT: the brief each Claude note was written from. Rebuilt on demand; private.
alrt_work/
# SPLC: the sentences Claude was given when it read a company's filings.
splc_work/
# OIL: the page as Claude was given it for each oil note, with your holdings.
oil_work/
# WCH: one stock as Claude was given it for a second opinion, with your book's fit.
wl_work/
# READ: the candidates and your holdings as Claude was given them for each scan and article.
# KAI: what Koers AI was sent for each turn (kai-* folders), your return on its scoreboard.
read_work/
# The weekly review's Claude note writes its material here (pf/weekly.py).
week_work/
# Claude Code's local settings for this folder (test servers, permissions).
.claude/

# --- OS ------------------------------------------------------------------
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store
